* The X following G() in the DEFINE prototype declares a function-local binding.
* F reads the currently active X while G is executing because the binding is dynamically scoped.
* Returning from G restores the previous X. RETURN yields the value stored in the function name.
    X = 1
    DEFINE('F()')
    DEFINE('G()X')
    OUTPUT = G()
    OUTPUT = X :(END)
F F = X :(RETURN)
G X = 2
    G = F() :(RETURN)
END
